          },
          {
            "document_hash": "c0e044580014a1113a75c9585c9aeda050551be17228a84b3ed53efc1748b8ce",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-c0e044580014-0000-0004"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 7,
              "start": 7
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Petitioner argues that a clearing futures commodity merchant (FCM) has standing to sue contract markets and clearing organizations under Section\u202f25(b)(1) of the Commodity Exchange Act for bad\u2011faith failure to enforce required rules."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "United States (Amicus Curiae)",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "c0e044580014a1113a75c9585c9aeda050551be17228a84b3ed53efc1748b8ce",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-c0e044580014-0000-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 20,
              "start": 20
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to United States (Amicus Curiae), according to United States (Amicus Curiae), the United States, as amicus curiae, suggests that the word \u201ctransaction\u201d in Section\u202f25(b)(1) should be read as limited to the purchase and sale of futures and options contracts."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Respondents (Mr. Stewart)",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "c0e044580014a1113a75c9585c9aeda050551be17228a84b3ed53efc1748b8ce",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-c0e044580014-0001-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 27,
              "start": 27
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Respondents (Mr. Stewart), according to Respondents (Mr. Stewart), respondent contends that the clearing FCM assumes direct contractual liability to the clearinghouse."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Petitioner (Mr. Pincus)",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "c0e044580014a1113a75c9585c9aeda050551be17228a84b3ed53efc1748b8ce",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-c0e044580014-0002-0003"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 45,
              "start": 45
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Petitioner (Mr. Pincus), according to Petitioner (Mr. Pincus), petitioner further argues that \u201con or subject to\u201d language in the statute refers to trades, and that Congress\u2019s technical substitution of registered entities does not change that meaning."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Petitioner (Mr. Pincus)",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "c0e044580014a1113a75c9585c9aeda050551be17228a84b3ed53efc1748b8ce",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-c0e044580014-0002-0004"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 49,
              "start": 49
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Petitioner warns that the lack of clarity about the statute creates two categories of harm, including uncertainty about how far back liability may extend."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Mr. Days",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "c0e044580014a1113a75c9585c9aeda050551be17228a84b3ed53efc1748b8ce",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-c0e044580014-0003-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 58,
              "start": 58
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Mr. Days, speaking for the petitioner, the clearing FCM is financially liable throughout the transaction process and that Congress intended the statute to protect the public and preserve market credibility."
      }
    ],
